Z||000009||theogre||09-24-2000||01:56 PM||||I missed what year they said it was.... nope. no cradel bushings in 88.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cheever2||09-24-2000||08:50 PM||||Get accustomed to that gas gauge thing.  It's the virus of the Fiero world.  The only fix I saw from one of these fine Fiero Forum folks was way too much trouble for my lazy bones.  Requires soldering too, and I've never done that successfully.  No hand coordination, I guess.  Ikan tipe tho.<BR>You might check out Alamo Area Fiero Owners, or Austin Fiero Club.  Over here we got Lone Star.  I like the Owners' Location Database too.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Carrolles||09-25-2000||09:39 AM||||Welcome to the world of Fieros and to this forum.  Try this site for a wealth of info.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>My gas gauge isn't quite that bad.  I usually reset the trip odometer whenever I fill up and monitor miles driven as a backup to the gauge.  Once I get around 125 to 150 miles I fillup.  I have an 85SE v-6 which has a smaller gas tank than yours.  Also if you have standard trans you have 5th gear and get better highway mileage than my 4spd.<P>Again welcome to the forum,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
